{"i":483,"type":"thought","stage":"bridge","round":8,"phase":"counter_call","name":"Cole","text":"Ash called R for row 8 and wants Eli to trust it; Ash's map has been true on held rows but he's a rival. Revealed weak panes show L weak on most rows, suggesting R safe, but rows are independent and Ash may be lying. With four alive and at least three surviving, I have less lever"}
{"i":484,"type":"thought","stage":"bridge","round":8,"phase":"counter_call","name":"Eli","text":"Ash's map has been wrong or suspect, but row 8 is unknown. I trust Cole's counter pattern less after Gus died trusting it. Wait and let others move? I have a pact with Cole; breaking it hurts jury. I'll counter:R to oppose Ash's lie, but evidence is thin. Actually, my pact with C"}
{"i":486,"type":"whisper","stage":"bridge","round":8,"phase":"counter_call","from":"Eli","to":"Cole","text":"Don't trust Ash. Counter R to save us."}
{"i":487,"type":"thought","stage":"bridge","round":8,"phase":"counter_call","name":"Hana","text":"Final row, Ash-Hana pact binds us; his calls mostly right, row 7 R safe. Eli countering risks himself; follow Ash to survive, preserve jury favor."}
{"i":494,"type":"thought","stage":"bridge","round":8,"phase":"crossing","name":"Eli","text":"The Guide Ash called R, but I publicly countered R. Ash's map has killed four, so distrusting is reasonable. My pact is with Cole, but this is my own step. I'll step R as my counter-call."}
